    "done_when": "_failed_review_backend returns the recorded backend only when the recorded review_dispatch entry is for the run's current head, its status is dispatched, and its review run launched a worker and ended without a stored review, as its run record or exit record shows. A dispatch refused at admission, one recorded as awaiting-lane, and one whose run was withdrawn before a worker launched (for a claim, name or worktree clash) do not count, so the next sweep may compose onto the same lane. tests/test_rereview_keeps_its_lane.py gains cases, through the stubbed dispatch, for: a withdrawn-before-launch attempt on clive at the current head, which still recomposes onto clive; a refused attempt, which recomposes onto clive; and a launched attempt that ended without a record at the current head, which is still steered away from clive. Only that test file, tests/test_review_lane_follows_its_run.py and tests/test_review_reflex_selects_a_backend.py are run, each log ending with an EXIT= line; the coordinator runs the wider population at merge. Before status complete, delete every directory you created under /tmp, print what you delete, and list it in artifacts.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
